 Approach, complexity & discussion — open after you solve 
 The approach
 Trim a conversation to fit a token budget while keeping the essentials. Always keep the system message , then keep the most recent turns that fit, dropping (or summarizing) the oldest until you are under budget. Count tokens , not messages, and trim at message boundaries.
 Complexity
 Time O(n) over the messages.
 Common mistakes
 Dropping the system message when the history gets long — it must always survive.
 Trimming by message count instead of token count, so you blow the budget on a few long messages.
 Cutting in the middle of a message rather than at a clean boundary.
 Where this shows up
 Token-budget trimming is core context engineering : every long-running agent must compact its history to stay under the context window without losing the system prompt or recent state. The “keep system plus the most recent turns that fit” rule is the baseline every chat and agent loop needs.

